//KNOWN BUG (Phase 8e-5 known limitation): OP_Box's null-sentinel
//optimization at VmExecutor.cpp:854 skips heap allocation when val==0
//and typeTag != RTK_String. This means a legitimate boxed int 0 in a
//List<int> stores heap-idx 0 (the null sentinel). When list.get(0)
//tries to unbox that null sentinel, OP_Unbox throws.
//
//Lock the current behavior so a future fix is observable. Fix requires
//design decision (see nlang-phase-8e-5-foreach-design.md "Known
//limitations" and brainstorming needed):
//  Option A — always allocate heap slot in OP_Box (drop null-sentinel
//             optimization; lose ability to distinguish Object o = null
//             from Object o = 0).
//  Option B — use a separate null sentinel distinct from any heap idx
//             (e.g., -1; requires checking every Object-typed load).
//  Option C — type-tag-aware boxing (only skip alloc for AST null
//             literal, not for runtime int 0).
int main() {
    List<int> nums = new List<int>();
    nums.add(0);
    nums.add(5);
    int x = nums.get(0);
    return x;
}
